            <ArticleTitle>Update on administration of anesthetics and psychoactive drugs for pain management in China.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.aat.2015.05.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1875-4597(15)00051-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anesthetics and psychoactive drugs could relieve diseases, if used properly. However, they can cause dependency, and their misuse or abuse could adversely affect people's health and social stability. For a long time, the Chinese government has been reinforcing the regulation on anesthetics and psychoactive drugs to ensure their legal and proper usage, and to prevent abuse. The state council issued 'the regulations on the administration of anesthetic drugs and psychotropic drugs' in 2005, based on which a legal system was established for administration of anesthetics and psychoactive drugs with the objectives of ensuring their legitimate medical utilization, and preventing illegal abuse.</AbstractText>
